Roger Books (books@nucmar.physics.fsu.edu) wrote:
: I've compiled nethack on my Ultrix system for X11.  Seems to run fine with
: one little problem.  When I get a text entry window I can't enter any
: text.  I'm using a sparc/1 for my X display if this makes any difference.

Looks to me like it might be a focus problem.  If it is, then you'll be able
to type text into a pop-up only after repositioning the mouse-pointer over
the text region, or even worse: by clicking in the window.

I recall that the nethack source contained some focus option in a makefile
or some other config file.  You should try changing that to see if it helps.

The repositioning mouse problem seems to occur when nethack tries to position
the popup such that the pointer is inside it in order to give you focus,
but the border decorations produced by your window manager shift the position
of the popup.

This can be avoided by configuring your window manager to have either no
borders, or equivalently zero-width borders.

Having to click to gain focus in a popup is even more frustrating, and if you
have this problem, again I suggest you look to reconfiguring your window
manager.

Finally, you might do what many nethackers do, and stick to windowtype:tty
It seems a bit faster, and although you might miss some neato colours and
graphics, you can still use the nh10 font in the window.

Hope this helps,

